smartctl
Usage: smartctl [-H|-a|-A] /dev/sdX   |   smartctl -t short /dev/sdX

Reads a drive's own SMART health data -- is it failing before you trust it with
data or wipe it? A one-line health verdict, the full attribute table, or kick
off a self-test.

	-H /dev/sdX   the overall health verdict (PASSED / FAILING)
	-a /dev/sdX   every attribute and the full report
	-A /dev/sdX   just the attribute values (pipe to `chart`)
	-t short /dev/sdX   start a short self-test

See also: ddrescue, chart
